# Certificate & verification security

## HMAC mechanism (§4)

1. Canonical string: `uniqueId|recipientName|eventId|clubId|issueDate(YYYY-MM-DD)|role`
2. Token = HMAC-SHA256 hex with `CERT_HMAC_SECRET`
3. QR/URL: `/v/{uniqueId}?t={token}`
4. Verify: recompute from **current DB fields**, compare with `timingSafeEqual`
5. Also accept tokens signed with `CERT_HMAC_SECRET_PREVIOUS` during rotation

## Public verification page

- Always live DB read (Rule 1)
- Require token; sequential ID alone must fail
- **Valid:** name, club, event, date, role/achievement, status — nothing else
- **Revoked:** only “This certificate has been revoked.” (no name/event/details)
- **Invalid / missing token:** generic failure — do not leak whether the ID exists beyond “not found” vs “bad token” if avoidable; never return email
- Rate-limit the public endpoint by IP when wiring API routes

## Schema / RLS

- Keep `clubId` on Certificate, Event, CertificateTemplate, AuditLog
- Never hard-delete certificates
- Admin dashboard queries must be club-scoped; RLS in `supabase/rls-policies.sql` is mandatory before production
- Public verify uses server-side Prisma / service role — not the anon key against Certificate tables

## Tests required (Rule 11)

Before merging changes here: valid token passes, tampered token fails, revoked display policy holds.
